# EMDR — page finish: redpen + writing-copy + frontend-design

Whenever you **create or change a page / screen / layout / user-facing UI** (marketing, `/app`, onboarding, auth, billing, modals, empty states), do **not** end the turn until you run this review.

**First:** load `.cursor/skills/nura-ui-designer/SKILL.md` for visual/system decisions (`/nura-ui-designer`).

## Required end review (in order)

1. **/redpen** (`~/.agents/skills/redpen/SKILL.md`) — truth, reader moment, no echo, no dead template lines; rewrite material defects.
2. **/writing-copy** (`~/.cursor/skills/writing-copy/SKILL.md`) — clarity over cleverness; one idea per block; CTA says what happens; microcopy is actionable.
3. **/frontend-design** (`~/.agents/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md`) — hierarchy, type scale, spacing, contrast; not a generic SaaS card; brand still reads as Nura (see `nura-brand`).

Also obey **nura-brand** (spoken Nura, no BLS jargon, pistachio tokens, marketing vs product type). On **marketing** pages, also obey **marketing-no-explain-copy** — no body paragraphs that explain; show with hierarchy, cards, and visuals.

## If anything fails the review

- **Propose** the concrete copy/layout changes (short redlines).
- **Apply** them in the same turn when you are shipping the page — do not leave only chat advice.
- Re-check the three skills after edits (light pass is enough).

## Pass criteria (quick)

- [ ] No repeated phrase across kicker / title / lead / CTA
- [ ] Marketing: no explanatory body copy (see **marketing-no-explain-copy**)
- [ ] A new user understands what to do in ~2 seconds
- [ ] Type and spacing are readable on mobile (~390×844)
- [ ] One clear primary action; secondary chrome does not compete
- [ ] Screen could not be mistaken for a random SaaS template after removing the lockup (or you have a deliberate Nura signature)

## Skip only when

- Pure API / DB / scripts / tests with **no** user-visible strings or layout
- Commit messages, changelog bullets, code comments

When writing copy outside a full page change, still use **redpen** (this rule + prior redpen-copy habit).
